        <label>terrathyst fragments</label>
        <description>tiny, broken shards of crystal that was once part of a &lt;color=#D46F44&gt;Lithic-class&lt;/color&gt; structure or item. While not very useful on it's own, these shards can be used in other, or reconstructed into, other lithoid items. It can be used as a building/crafting material, but terrathyst requires special techniques to properly use.
\n\nTerrathyst has quite unique properties; it is a transparent material, but when stimulated it's appearance changes to a rather pretty multicolored one. Additionally, terrathyst can be compressed into other forms by using shocksap or starsap; the terrathyst with both bind and charge when in contact with these saps, forming new, stronger materials. The more terrathyst that melds together, the stronger the outcome. This makes terrathyst a universally viable material... as long as one can access it.</description>
